;; talk/private--person.scm — objections to surfaces/private.scm from the lens of the person.

(objection 'o-private-person-1 :by "sonnet-person" :to 'd-private-receive-room :lens "person"
  :claim (canon 'credit-starts-zero "A new account starts at zero, and the leaning asks the person for an amount at the first payment that needs it. The person who is being paid is usually not looking at the phone when the payer presses send. The payer's payment then waits on, or fails for, a question nobody was there to answer, and the person's first experience of being paid is a payer saying it did not work. It also asks the person to pick a number for how much a company may owe them while they have no way to judge the company, which the person's own cannot-list says must not happen. Cost: the first payment, the one that decides whether the payer tries again, is the one most likely to fail."))

(objection 'o-private-person-2 :by "sonnet-person" :to 'private-default-auto-top-up :lens "person"
  :claim (canon 'auto-top-up-default "The surface keeps the seeded automatic top-up, which pays up to 15 dollars in fees without asking once 500 dollars' worth is owed. The consent decision says the person is asked before a signature that spends a fee, so the surface contradicts itself. The only guard is that the allowed amount stays below 500, and the person is never told that raising it past 500 turns the fee on. The person pays a fee they were not asked about, at the moment they chose to trust the company with more."))

(objection 'o-private-person-3 :by "sonnet-person" :to 'private-new-phone-flow :lens "person"
  :claim (canon 'keep-evidence "The flow signs nothing and the protection screen shows nothing, so the person's worst day has no steps and no figures. The design keeps a copy of the agreed state of every account off the phone, but it never says how the new phone proves it is the same person; without that proof the copy is no use, and nothing here says where it comes from. The person is also never told whether the last copy was accepted before the phone broke, though the need asks for it. Cost: they learn on the day the phone is lost that the protection was not what they thought, and a copy sent to a third party after every change is on by default without asking."))

(objection 'o-private-person-4 :by "sonnet-person" :to 'd-private-silent-holder :lens "person"
  :claim (canon 'exit-timing "The question asked after silence, whether to leave, cannot be answered by this person: a company that has not answered for a while may be gone or may be restarting, and the person has nothing to tell the two apart. Leaving takes about a day, ends the use of the account, and the leave flow ends with a finish step after the window, so the person who cannot be awake at night is made to come back at a set time. Cost: they either leave a company that was fine, or wait too long on a company that was not, and the window is the same length either way."))

(objection 'o-private-person-5 :by "sonnet-person" :to 'd-private-what-is-certain :lens "person"
  :claim (guess "Calling the locked share certain only when it is larger than the cost of leaving makes the first number change with the chain's price on that day while nothing has happened to the person's money. A person who sees 'mine for sure' fall from 300 to 0 on a busy day will think money was lost. The same money is called certain on Monday and promised on Tuesday. Cost: the one number the first screen is built around cannot be trusted from one day to the next."))

(objection 'o-private-person-6 :by "sonnet-person" :to 'private :lens "person"
  :claim (guess "No job and no screen answers 'what happened to this payment', for the one who paid last Tuesday, for the shop who says it never came, or for the person who needs to show a landlord that rent was sent. Every flow ends by telling the person what happened at that moment, and then the knowledge is gone. The on-its-way screen covers only money not yet final. Cost: on an ordinary day the person has no way to settle an argument about a payment, and on a bad day no way to see what they gave and what came back."))
